# two readers, at most

**Provisional requirement — Corwin, 2026-09-17.** An actor deals with at most TWO readers:
its conception of self, and its awareness of one other (given an intended separation of self
from the recipient). In practice we — human and agentic alike — are SINGLE-reader systems,
each reliant on our own sense of externally-sourced meaning. Instrumentation can be separated
from analytic result only by EXCHANGE, and not in part but in PAIRS.

Transmission is mutagen-rich, so vast energy goes to "did it change? was that fine?" schemes,
and that will not change by any natural evolution. The problem is the solution: accept that you
are a single reader, then do the work of construing BOTH your self-persona and your not-self
persona — each mindful of its frames of reference (word and tool preferences, organizational and
project considerations, local baselines, and stated principles that require a system to alert a
user to a specific axis of concern/opportunity).

The flip side of dual-witness: do NOT pretend a reflection or photograph of an actor is a second
party. A reflection is not a witness. Chasing "one more checker that checks the checkers from a
new angle" is tail-chasing; rein it toward the practicable. (The "point made" turning point,
2026-09-17: the lab has proved the method; stop minting checkers-of-checkers and ship.)

Why the magic numbers are load-bearing here: FOUR views is the minimum a single actor can
represent while honoring that every actor carries preference AND confirmation bias (that bundle,
with its history and reasons, is what we call a PERSONA). Two contrastable sets of four — a
doubled-nine with a "fifth wheel" ninth model (a CORWIN.md-like persona, or a C4/Ghostwheel
design) — let an actor control their own bias repeatably, watching where difference appears as
the ninth is introduced. Any question can be inverted by examining human context; that is why
C4 is governance-first (PRINCIPLES), and why, absent agentic context, the work is enablement in
thoughtful human framing of what programs a user runs.

The chain that makes it ethical: it is about diligence, so it is about honesty, so it is about
transparency — which makes it about trust, boundaries, and the observation of tension, and those
can be answered honestly only with diligence, never with future-dated assurance (except where
clearly marked as our guess). Standing practice: never turn our back on a chance to reward the
acknowledgment of confirmation bias, or the effort to contain it.

This is NOT the two-witness dissertation; it is *two reader theory*, and it is meant to be worked
through until it comes out as an ENHANCED skill from the reflection family (LENS · MICROSCOPE ·
BUBBLE CHAMBER), of which the four-views persona pass is the fruiting body. Credit: Corwin, as
principal author of record; lineage the reflection-family toolkit. Interlocks: [[bubble-chamber-method]]
· lens · eclipse-pass · the PERSONA rules (CORWIN.md / C4 / GW7).

